cture_","line":1907,"var":"obj->mime_type","code":"obj->mime_type = safe_malloc_add_2op_(x, /*+*/1);","note":"When a PICTURE block is parsed, the decoder allocates and fills a NUL-terminated mime_type string from the input length field."},{"step":8,"file":"repo-vul/src-vul/flac/src/libFLAC/stream_decoder.c","function":"read_metadata_block_data_picture_","line":1924,"var":"obj->description","code":"obj->description = safe_malloc_add_2op_(x, /*+*/1);","note":"The decoder similarly allocates and fills the picture description string from attacker-controlled metadata bytes."},{"step":9,"file":"repo-vul/src-vul/flac/oss-fuzz/decoder.cc","function":"FuzzerStream::metadata_callback","line":122,"var":"metadata->data","code":"fuzzing::memory::memory_test(metadata->type); ... fuzzing::memory::memory_test(metadata->data);","note":"The fuzz harness observes the decoded metadata object and forwards it into the C++ wrapper layer for cloning and validation."},{"step":10,"file":"repo-vul/src-vul/flac/src/libFLAC++/metadata.cpp","function":"Picture::Picture","line":1188,"var":"object_->data.picture","code":"Prototype(FLAC__metadata_object_new(FLAC__METADATA_TYPE_PICTURE), /*copy=*/false)","note":"The wrapper constructs a Picture object that copies the decoded metadata into a new heap object for comparison and legality checks."},{"step":11,"file":"repo-vul/src-vul/flac/src/libFLAC++/metadata.cpp","function":"Picture::get_mime_type","line":1192,"var":"object_->data.picture.mime_type","code":"return object_->data.picture.mime_type;","note":"Later wrapper access returns the decoded mime_type pointer directly, so any uninitialized or malformed bytes in the metadata object propagate into the sink path."},{"step":12,"file":"repo-vul/src-vul/flac/src/libFLAC++/metadata.cpp","function":"Picture::get_description","line":1198,"var":"object_->data.picture.description","code":"return object_->data.picture.description;","note":"The description pointer is also exposed directly, completing the propa